### Neutron Star Binary Assembly Rates

To calculate the encounter rate within the cluster we assume NSs are distributed homogeneously within the core, with fractional number f_{\\rm ns}, total number density n_{\\rm c}, and binary fraction b_{\\rm ns}. We further assume that the stars follow a Maxwellian velocity distribution function with dispersion \\sigma_{\\rm c}. We calculate a fiducial encounter rate \\xi_{\\rm ns} for individual clusters provided a distance of closest approach R_{\\rm min}(e.g. Lee et al., 2010),

\\xi_{\\rm ns}=3\\times 10^{-3}\\,{\\rm Gyr}^{-1}f_{\\rm ns}^{2}\\left( \\frac{n_{\\rm c}}{10^{6}\\ {\\rm pc}^{-3}}\\right)^{2}\\left(\\frac{r_{\\rm c}}{0.1\\ {\\rm pc }}\\right)^{3}\\times\\\\ \\left(\\frac{\\sigma_{\\rm c}}{20\\ {\\rm km\\,s}^{-1}}\\right)^{-1}\\left( \\frac{M_{\\rm ns}}{1.4\\ {\\rm M}_{\\odot}}\\right)\\left(\\frac{R_{\\rm min}}{10\\ {\\rm km}} \\right). 

